@owner: mason
@stability: stable
@since: 2026-06-09
@reviewed: 2026-06-09

Feature: Share Link Mutations
  "Creates and updates share symlinks and patches the authoritative manifest without moving blob bytes."

  Provides:
    - links.Service @source("symbol:Service")
    - links.NewService @source("symbol:NewService")
    - links.ShareRequest @source("symbol:ShareRequest")
    - links.ShareResult @source("symbol:ShareResult")
    - links.Service.EnsureShare @source("symbol:EnsureShare")
    - links.MoveRequest @source("symbol:MoveRequest")
    - links.MoveResult @source("symbol:MoveResult")
    - links.Service.Move @source("symbol:Move")
    - links.CopyRequest @source("symbol:CopyRequest")
    - links.CopyResult @source("symbol:CopyResult")
    - links.Service.Copy @source("symbol:Copy")
    - links.RemoveRequest @source("symbol:RemoveRequest")
    - links.RemoveResult @source("symbol:RemoveResult")
    - links.Service.Remove @source("symbol:Remove")
    - links.EndpointRequest @source("symbol:EndpointRequest")
    - links.EndpointResult @source("symbol:EndpointResult")
    - links.Service.Disable @source("symbol:Disable")
    - links.Service.Enable @source("symbol:Enable")
    - links.PruneRequest @source("symbol:PruneRequest")
    - links.PruneResult @source("symbol:PruneResult")
    - links.Service.Prune @source("symbol:Prune")

  Consumes:
    - remote.ManifestStore
    - remote.EnsureSafeSymlink
    - domain.Manifest.DecideShare
    - domain.Manifest.OrphanedBlobs
    - domain.MintSlug

  Invariants:
    - EnsureShare MUST require the blob to already exist in the manifest (two-phase share)
    - New shares MUST mint a slug, reserve it, and create object-path plus canonical and bare slug symlinks
    - Repoint MUST update symlinks only for endpoints still in EndpointOK state
    - Move MUST re-home only the object-path endpoint and leave the slug endpoint unchanged
    - Copy MUST create a new share with a fresh slug over the same blob without moving bytes
    - Remove MUST act on the referenced endpoint only; reserved slugs MUST NOT be unreserved
    - Disable and Enable MUST toggle one endpoint symmetrically; disabled endpoints MUST still count toward blob references
    - Prune MUST report orphans without Confirm and MUST update the manifest before deleting blob files when confirmed
    - Symlink targets MUST stay relative to each link parent directory under the site root
    - Remote symlink changes MUST complete or roll back before manifest writes fail visibly to the caller

  OutOfScope:
    - Blob byte upload (owned by the share package)
    - CLI rendering and target resolution (owned by internal/cli)

  Scenario (happy-path): Create new share
    Given a manifest with the blob recorded but no share at the object path
    When EnsureShare runs
    Then Action is ShareCreate, symlinks are written, and manifest is committed

  Scenario (happy-path): Move object path
    Given a share with an active object-path endpoint
    When Move runs to an unused destination
    Then the slug endpoint is unchanged and the object-path symlink is re-homed

  Scenario (happy-path): Copy share
    Given a share referenced by either endpoint
    When Copy runs to an unused destination
    Then a new share with a new slug points at the same blob and the source share is untouched

  Scenario (happy-path): Disable endpoint
    Given an enabled endpoint
    When Disable runs
    Then symlinks are removed before the manifest is marked disabled

  Scenario (happy-path): Prune confirmed
    Given orphaned blobs in the manifest
    When Prune runs with Confirm
    Then manifest entries are removed before blob files are deleted

  Scenario (negative): Blob not uploaded
    Given a blob key absent from manifest.Blobs
    When EnsureShare runs
    Then it returns an error instructing the caller to upload first
